preConditionHook:
// The workhorse measured move: height = the high-low span of the refBars bars
// that produced the breakout, projected a multiple of itself beyond the broken
// extreme. Spike, channel, trading range, wedge, triangle, flag, double
// top/bottom and head-and-shoulders are all this same arithmetic; the
// projection anchor coincides for every one of them, because the level broken
// IS the window's own extreme.
// EL Highest(high[1], refBars) / Lowest(low[1], refBars): the window ENDS ONE
// BAR AGO, bars 1..refBars, so the signal bar cannot define its own pattern.
// Extremes is EL SOURCE -- seeded on the window's first bar, strict comparison
// so a tie keeps the earliest bar, carrying the relational tolerance, hence
// el_gt/el_lt rather than >/<.
// Two double toggles select the book's alternate anchor pair: startFromOpen
// replaces the window's far side with the open of its first bar, endAtClose
// replaces the near side with the close of its last bar and anchors the
// projection there.
// Every subscript is read UNCONDITIONALLY -- EasyLanguage does not
// short-circuit (EL_LogicalEval_Probe), so Max Bars Back must cover refBars on
// every bar -- and only the projection is frozen at entry. BarsSinceEntry() is
// 0 on the fill bar and 0 while flat (VERIFIED), so the capture re-arms on
// every flat bar. Frozen at entry, not re-read every bar, which is what
// separates it from AtrProfitTarget's running distance.
// tolerancePoints is in PRICE UNITS: the source's 'tested within one tick'
// convention cannot be spelled in ticks while MinMove / PriceScale are UNKNOWN.
winHigh = high[1];
winLow = low[1];
for (int i = 2; i <= (int)refBars; ++i) {
    if (el_gt(high[i], winHigh)) winHigh = high[i];
    if (el_lt(low[i], winLow)) winLow = low[i];
}
longTop = winHigh;
longBot = winLow;
shortTop = winHigh;
shortBot = winLow;
if (el_gt(startFromOpen, 0.0)) {
    longBot = open[refBars];
    shortTop = open[refBars];
}
if (el_gt(endAtClose, 0.0)) {
    longTop = close[1];
    shortBot = close[1];
}
if (el_eq((double)ctx.BarsSinceEntry(), 0.0)) {
    targetLong = longTop + multiple * (longTop - longBot);
    targetShort = shortBot - multiple * (shortTop - shortBot);
}
